div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The world is wide enough for them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, when there comes that time when the world suddenly shrinks...<br /> <br /> Oof, someone's gonna have a bad time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T02:45:45-07:00","id":944766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/942976-it-s-alive-promethean-2e-is-here?p=944680#post944680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The world is wide enough for them all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It just gets weird at times that the &quot;monster-hunting&quot; corps we have are disproportionately pharmaceutical companies. Obviously that makes important thematic sense here! And Cheiron was first. But I kind of feel like Last Dynasty or &quot;Luminous Labs&quot; (the Demon experimenting wing of Deva) could have gone different directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T17:45:06-07:00","id":945181,"title":"","content":"Oh Hovel, am I wrong or does this Merit seem to be designed to help facilitate, non nomadic Promethean Chars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:23:01-07:00","id":945201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/942976-it-s-alive-promethean-2e-is-here?p=945181#post945181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh Hovel, am I wrong or does this Merit seem to be designed to help facilitate, non nomadic Promethean Chars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Allowing for non-nomadic Chronicles was a major design goal, if I recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:23:45-07:00","id":945202,"title":"","content":"So, uh. Ten Refinement New Dawn. Transhuman Redemption.EDIT: Okay, transhuman might be pushing it too far, since a lot of the human condition is still present. STILL.<br /> <br /> The conversations from here on are going to be <i>interesting.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-06-2016, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T19:08:47-07:00","id":945222,"title":"","content":"Yeah; if I have a problem with any one aspect of the new New Dawn mechanics, that's it: \u201ckeep one Alembic that you fixed in your previous life\u201d is nice as an <i>option</i>; but I'd rather there be alternatives to that, some of which are supernatural (e.g., \u201cyou get to Redeem with a suitable lesser template\u201d or \u201cyou get to trade in your fixed Alembics for Supernatural Merits\u201d) and some which aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:30:04-07:00","id":945254,"title":"","content":"I'm personally cool with it, but it makes certain conversations much harder to be had, which makes me giggle.<br /> <br /> You know, ignoring the people who never read the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:35:52-07:00","id":945256,"title":"","content":"Im glad we dont see the Dozen and one Alternatives to the New Dawn, we keep hearing people wanting.<br /> <br /> no offense to them, but every paragraph spent on &quot;Giving us options&quot; is one that could have gone to exploring the New Dawn<br /> <br /> One thing I do miss, is it being possible in 1st edition to be a Centimeti and still on the pilgrimage, by deconstructing humanity, and understanding that your completely inhuman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T22:40:57-07:00","id":945300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/942976-it-s-alive-promethean-2e-is-here?p=943083#post943083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else as excited about the Lost Lineages as I am? Here's hoping we see the old fire lineage in the Dark Eras Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's been confirmed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T22:53:16-07:00","id":945304,"title":"","content":"*headcanon*. As the five Complex Refinements had to have original creators, they have historic associations with the five elemental Lineages based on the legends of the Pilgrims that first discovered and taught them.<br /> <br /> Aes - Tammuz<br /> Argentum - Ulgan<br /> Cobalus - Galatea<br /> Mercuris - Osiris<br /> Phosphorum - &quot;Prophet&quot;<br /> <br /> Some Unfleshed, Extempora, and Wretched have under this thinking sought to discover if there may be other Aspects of Azoth for their Lineages to discover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T15:14:16-07:00","id":945698,"title":"","content":"Rules question: I can't seem to find for long it takes to change refinements. Did it get smoothed over, or am I just missing something obvious?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T15:30:39-07:00","id":945709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/942976-it-s-alive-promethean-2e-is-here?p=945698#post945698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules question: I can't seem to find for long it takes to change refinements. Did it get smoothed over, or am I just missing something obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it is variable now, between a week and a few months. Except Stannum, which you can still drop into immediately at any time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T18:55:38-07:00","id":945804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/942976-it-s-alive-promethean-2e-is-here?p=945304#post945304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*headcanon*. As the five Complex Refinements had to have original creators, they have historic associations with the five elemental Lineages based on the legends of the Pilgrims that first discovered and taught them.<br /> <br /> Aes - Tammuz<br /> Argentum - Ulgan<br /> Cobalus - Galatea<br /> Mercuris - Osiris<br /> Phosphorum - &quot;Prophet&quot;<br /> <br /> Some Unfleshed, Extempora, and Wretched have under this thinking sought to discover if there may be other Aspects of Azoth for their Lineages to discover.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooh. Now, that I may grab to expand if I ever get to do a PG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T00:09:44-07:00","id":945996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/942976-it-s-alive-promethean-2e-is-here?p=945202#post945202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh. Ten Refinement New Dawn. Transhuman Redemption.EDIT: Okay, transhuman might be pushing it too far, since a lot of the human condition is still present. STILL.<br /> <br /> The conversations from here on are going to be <i>interesting.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that if you get an exceptional success on the New Dawn roll *and* have done all ten Refinements already, the exceptional roll could instead grant the bestowment you had as a Promethean (or alternatively an additional social advantage if you choose not to remember). It fits into the progression of boons you get the more Refinements you earn.<br /> <br /> On a different note, it is worth mentioning that if you choose to remember and get the Alembic and/or anything else supernatural, you are also a guaranteed Sleepwalker. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 08-08-2016, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:18:01-07:00","id":946664,"title":"","content":"Alright, I finally read the first parts up to the transmutations of chapter 3. Mechanical Discussion are always more difficult for me to read but I did like some of the differences entailed in the template that is with creating a character that is a Promethean.<br /> <br /> What I really enjoy about RPGs in general especially as it is related to storytelling is the conveyance of ideas within frameworks. Frameworks that are interpreted differently depending on both the taleteller and the listener. Hence mechanics that help with this is something I always have liked. The Pilgrimage mechanic and the use of milestones and vitriol experience.<br /> <br /> I don't really enjoy the aspiration and xp system of chronicles of darkness games in general simply because it feels like I am moving at a constant pace to where I want to go. There is something stagnant about that approach. I want to start off sprinting and then slow down and get tired. Therefore I look forward to how pilgramage mechanics change that for me in the game when I read the later chapter discussing that in detail.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 08-08-2016, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T01:34:07-07:00","id":946808,"title":"","content":"Interesting... with Plumbum being a basic Refinement, and Mercurius being complex (a move I either predicted or suggested myself on this forum), the unavoidable result is a slight lack of symmetry in associated Transmutations, as Disquietism appears twice in the Basic Refinements and nowhere in the Complex, and Vulcanus appears twice in the Complex Refinements and nowhere in the Basic.<br /> <br /> If Plumbum was Complex, and Mercurius was Basic, you'd have perfect symmetry where every Refinement paired one Transmutation that appears once in each set with one completely unique Transmutation.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say Plumbum should be Complex and Mercurius should be Basic - OF COURSE LEAD SHOULD BE BASIC! Approaching the Pilgrimage from the position &quot;What am I?&quot; is a naturally plausible first step!<br /> <br /> So I guess it just says something special about Disquietism as deeply rooted in the baser nature of the Promethean condition, and Vulcanus as being inherently something that only is reached through exploring higher mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:42:06-07:00","id":947432,"title":"","content":"So what makes the most sense for a Promethean pursuing the memories and connections of their body's previous identity/identities?<br /> <br /> Aurum (role depending on the person and their connections)<br /> <br /> Plumbum (probably a new Role, focusing on the bodily side of their &quot;Origin&quot;)<br /> <br /> An entirely new Refinement focusing on that specific theme?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:12:05-07:00","id":947507,"title":"","content":"There's room in plenty of Refinements for that exploration. Aurum and Plumbum are obvious. A Cuprum might spend time alone with her thoughts to try and separate what is hers from what is her previous life's. An Argentum might seek out the ghost of his previous inhabitant, or his anchors, or other echoes in the Underworld. A Cobalus might try to purge himself of these remnants. An Aes might feel some filial obligation to his body's relatives and friends. A Stannum, like the Cuprum and the Cobalus, might believe her Torment is influenced by the previous incarnation. A Ferrum might be troubled by the scars and tattoos she was raised with. Mercurius and Phosphorum might have less appeal to such a seeker, but the latter may might want to overcome the fears or even death that befell hir predecessor. .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T07:21:39-07:00","id":950545,"title":"","content":"I've posted my own reviews for those interested:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product_reviews_info.php?&amp;reviews_id=153762&amp;products_id=189395\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/themes/dtrpg/site-logo-redesignd.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product_reviews_info.php?&amp;reviews_id=153762&amp;products_id=189395\" target=\"_blank\"> DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product_reviews_info.php?&amp;reviews_id=153762&amp;products_id=189395\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product_reviews_info.php?&amp;reviews_id=153762&amp;products_id=189395 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> TL;DR: solid overall, though I would have done a few things differently. Still a very solid book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","val